t1a15-mandelbrot-prompt-fred.html <br>


Make a single-page full-screen HTML file with minimal inline CSS for a vibrant, zoomable Mandelbrot fractal.<br>

Requirements:<br>
1. Use an HTML5 canvas that fills the entire window with a black background.<br>
2. Render the Mandelbrot fractal with smooth, vibrant color cycling that stays vivid as you zoom in deeper.<br>
3. Show a dashed preview rectangle that tracks the mouse cursor, showing the exact region that will fill the screen on the next click.<br>
4. Allow the mouse wheel to dynamically resize the preview box (and zoom scaling factor).<br>
5. Clicking the canvas zooms into the fractal centered on the mouse position using the preview box scale.<br>
6. Add a clickable hint box in the top-left corner that toggles an info modal explaining how the fractal is generated using the formula Z_n+1 = Z_n^2 + C.<br>
7. Use descriptive camelCase JavaScript variables and functions starting with "my", async/await, and direct property assignments (like onclick/onwheel) instead of addEventListener where possible.<br>
